// OmniFlow batch 219 - Knowledge Base: PDF / Word (.docx) upload + scheduled re-fetch of web pages.
// (Replaces add_batch_kb_files_refresh_219.mjs - that download arrived EMPTY (0 bytes) on the laptop.)
//
// Run from the WEBSITE repo root (the folder that contains OmniFlow-Control-Plane/):
//     node kb_pdf_word_autorefresh_219.mjs
// Safe to run twice (second run says "already"). Old copies are kept as *.pre_219.bak.
//
// What it does:
//  * Control Plane: new portal_kb_files.py (PDF via pypdf, DOCX via stdlib zip/xml; size / page / time limits from env),
//    portal_knowledge.py (POST /kb/extract - human-only, stores nothing; per-source auto_refresh for web pages;
//    background refresh = new version as 'system', publication state never changed -> auto-publish lock kept;
//    chunker keeps list items / table rows out of headings), connector_api.py (tick kicks the refresh job, fail-soft),
//    requirements.txt += pypdf.
//  * Website: BFF /api/omniflow/portal/kb/extract, auto_refresh + filename forwarding, Knowledge card
//    (PDF/Word upload -> review text -> add as draft; Upload new version; Auto-refresh toggle with consent).
//  * Tests: tools/cp-testrig/test_kb_files.py (80 checks) + updated pins in test_knowledge.py / test_app_boot.py.
//
// Env (optional, defaults shown): OF_KB_FILE_BYTES_MAX=3000000 OF_KB_PDF_PAGES_MAX=300 OF_KB_EXTRACT_SECONDS=20
//   OF_KB_DOCX_PART_BYTES_MAX=30000000 OF_KB_AUTO_REFRESH_HOURS=168 OF_KB_REFRESH_BATCH=3 OF_KB_REFRESH_TICK_SECONDS=900
//
// After running: npm run build -> cd OmniFlow-Control-Plane -> git add -A -> commit -> push -> cd .. -> git add -A -> commit -> push
